# **Open SWE Repository Analysis**

## **1. Project Identity & Purpose**

**What it is:** Open SWE is an open-source framework for building organizational internal coding agents — agentic tools that automatically handle software engineering tasks (code changes, refactoring, bug fixes, CI/CD troubleshooting) and can be invoked from Slack, Linear tickets, GitHub PR comments, or a web dashboard.

**Problem domain:** Coding agent automation with enterprise-grade safety, sandboxing, and control. It's inspired by internal systems at Stripe (Minions), Ramp (Inspect), and Coinbase (Cloudbot) but open-sourced and composable on top of LangGraph + Deep Agents.

