## **9. Memory & Context Management**

### **Short-Term (Working Memory)**

- **Agent state:** Standard LangChain message list in graph state
- **Per-turn checkpoint:** Stored in LangGraph checkpointer (TTL 12 hours by default, [langgraph.json](langgraph.json) line ~16)
- **Sandbox worktree:** All files edited/created live in sandbox; agent reads/modifies them across turns
- **Turn diffs:** `refs/open-swe/turns/<user-message-id>` git refs record worktree state at run start for dashboard changed-files view ([agent/utils/turn_checkpoint.py](agent/utils/turn_checkpoint.py))

### **Long-Term (Persistent Storage)**

- **LangGraph store:** Persists thread metadata (thread_id → model, repo, owner, sandbox_id, timestamps)
- **LangSmith:** Trace logs and run history (if `LANGSMITH_API_KEY` set)
- **Dashboard database:** User profiles, repo access, enabled repos, team settings (exact DB technology not specified; likely PostgreSQL in deployment)
- **Review findings:** Stored in LangGraph store under namespace `["review_findings", pr_key]` ([agent/review/findings.py](agent/review/findings.py))

### **Context Truncation & Summarization**

- **Model call recursion limit:** `DEFAULT_RECURSION_LIMIT = 9_999` ([agent/runtime/constants.py](agent/runtime/constants.py) line 4); actual agent limit capped at `MODEL_CALL_RECURSION_LIMIT = 5_000`
- **Message queue injection:** Recent messages (Linear comments, Slack replies) injected before each model call via `check_message_queue_before_model` to keep history fresh
- **No automatic summarization:** Agent responsible for keeping own context; relies on model's context window and LLM's ability to compress history
- **Offloading large results:** Tool outputs that exceed inline limits are written to sandbox and referenced by path ([agent/tools/_sandbox_output.py](agent/tools/_sandbox_output.py))

### **Sandbox Persistence Strategy**

- **One sandbox per thread, persistent across turns** — Reused/reconnected on each invocation
- **Reconnection logic:** [agent/utils/sandbox_state.py](agent/utils/sandbox_state.py) `ensure_sandbox_for_thread` handles three cases:
  1. Cached in memory → ping (`echo ok`)
  2. Metadata has ID but not cached → reconnect
  3. No ID → create new sandbox
- **Sandbox as context:** All uncommitted code edits, git branches, temporary files preserved per thread

