## **13. Sandboxing & Safety**

### **Sandbox Providers**

Six pluggable providers (configurable via `SANDBOX_TYPE` env var):

| Provider | Isolation | Speed | Cold Start | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **LangSmith** (default) | Cloud VM | Fast | ~30s–1m | Persistent, GitHub proxy built-in |
| **Modal** | Serverless container | Fast | <10s | Pre-warmed; stateless |
| **Daytona** | Cloud container | Medium | ~30s | Dev-friendly; open-source |
| **Runloop** | Cloud sandbox | Medium | ~20s | Optimized for agent tasks |
| **E2B** | Cloud sandbox | Medium | ~10–30s | JavaScript/Python support |
| **Local** | Host shell | Instant | 0s | Dev only; no isolation (warning) |

**Default:** LangSmith; configured via `DEFAULT_SANDBOX_SNAPSHOT_ID` UUID.

**Source:** [agent/utils/sandbox.py](agent/utils/sandbox.py) line ~40; [agent/integrations/](agent/integrations/) provider files; [docs/CUSTOMIZATION.md](docs/CUSTOMIZATION.md) line ~60.

### **GitHub Proxy**

- **Mechanism:** LangSmith sandbox proxy intercepts git and API traffic to `github.com` and `api.github.com`
- **Auth injection:** Basic auth (git operations) and Bearer auth (API/`gh` CLI) injected from GitHub App installation token, minted at runtime
- **No token in sandbox:** Agent runs plain `gh <command>` without storing credentials
- **Auto-refresh:** `refresh_github_proxy_before_model` middleware refreshes proxy token before each model call

**Source:** [agent/integrations/langsmith.py](agent/integrations/langsmith.py) `_configure_github_proxy`; [agent/middleware/refresh_github_proxy.py](agent/middleware/refresh_github_proxy.py).

### **Filesystem Jails**

- **Root restriction:** Sandbox root defined per provider; all file operations confined to root
- **Deep Agents FilesystemBackend:** Validates paths; blocks `..` escapes and absolute paths outside root
- **Sandbox backend protocol:** All file ops routed through backend's `read_file`, `write_file`, `execute` methods (no raw OS access from agent)

### **Network Policies**

- **Egress:** Sandbox can call GitHub API (proxied), fetch URLs, call LLMs, post to Slack/Linear
- **Ingress:** No inbound listening; webhooks land on fastapi server, not in sandbox
- **Secrets:** No credentials stored in sandbox; injected via proxy or env-var at runtime

### **Secret Handling**

- **User GitHub tokens:** Stored encrypted at rest in dashboard database; decrypted only when needed for OAuth operations or PR attribution
- **GitHub App credentials:** Only in deployment environment; never in sandbox
- **Observability keys** (Datadog, LangSmith, Corridor): Kept in LangGraph server process; never sent to sandbox
- **Encryption:** `cryptography` library ([pyproject.toml](pyproject.toml) line 11) used for at-rest encryption

