## **Summary: Key Architectural Decisions**

| Decision | Rationale | Impact |
|---|---|---|
| **Composed on Deep Agents + LangGraph** | Upgrade path; don't fork OpenCode/Goose | Easier to pull upstream improvements |
| **One persistent sandbox per thread** | Preserves uncommitted work; simpler UX | State persists across turns; requires careful reconnection logic |
| **Curated small tool list (~25)** | Quality over quantity; less confusion | Less flexibility; fewer built-in tools than competitors |
| **Middleware stack ordering** | Fine-grained control over execution | Fragile; reordering breaks things; hard to extend |
| **Plan mode as workflow** | User review before code changes | Slower; more interaction; safer |
| **Deterministic thread IDs** | Idempotent follow-ups | Slightly complex ID derivation per-surface |
| **GitHub proxy for sandbox auth** | No credentials in sandbox; less risk | Extra hop; potential latency |
| **Reviewer as separate graph** | Read-only specialized agent | Parallel to main agent; adds complexity |
| **LangGraph store for state** | Built-in persistence + checkpointing | Tight coupling to LangGraph; not portable |

